      "timestamp_raw": "May 9, 2016 16:29:36 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "Sorry Eric, totally missed this request.  Technically, clone M is pictured somewhere below, haha!  I'll see if it's worth photographing and if so, will snap a couple of shots.<br/><br/>some new pics of various rubricorpora Liberty Co, FL clones, taken 5/8/16:<br/><img src=\"https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7148/26920323385_1ba5682e71_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7283/26920328805_900d105381_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>Hard to tell from this pic, but this clone has a super-dooper gigantea lid:<br/><img src=\"https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7685/26852866041_7d322704ea_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>Same giant lidded clone:<br/><img src=\"https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7491/26826703232_28f8fa3646_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>These got pretty big this year, the tall one pictured below is almost 3':<br/><img src=\"https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7108/26852809341_c8189db697_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7635/26826696842_92f9e5ffda_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7700/26852817411_970734b4f4_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>and a group shot of some outstanding clones, some of which I gotta photodocument soon.  There's an individual from the Lxbest clonecross  that is solid red:<br/><img src=\"https://farm8.staticflickr.com/7620/26887007546_1d50ed3be8_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
